WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.240
A person calling a mental health helpline
suddenly trails off

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.240
mid-sentence, entirely unable to finish
their current thought.

3
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.440
To a human listener, there is a distinct
ambiguity in

4
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.480
that dead air.

5
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.840
The caller might have simply lost a
specific word, they

6
00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.800
might have lost their entire train of
thought, or they

7
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.440
might be slipping into a genuine crisis.

8
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.560
Standard voice bots fail in this exact
gap.

9
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.880
They interpret any word-finding pause as a
turn boundary, assuming

10
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.080
the speaker is finished and prematurely
cut the user off

11
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.240
to deliver their automated reply.

12
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.760
Even if the system waits to listen,
standard language models

13
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.880
struggle to interpret neurodivergent
speech patterns.

14
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:46.240
They cannot reliably differentiate between
the hyperbole of rejection-sensitive dysphoria,

15
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.560
where a minor setback feels catastrophic,
and the actual alarming

16
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.720
language of a true emergency.

17
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.800
Leaving a large language model to
probabilistically guess whether someone

18
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.440
is experiencing everyday burnout or an
immediate threat to their

19
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:02.680
life is an unacceptable risk.

20
00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.520
To build a system that actually serves
ADHD users, the

21
00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:09.720
engineering must map directly to their
neurology.

22
00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.720
Cognitive limits have to be treated as
rigid design constraints.

23
00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:17.400
Because working memory is finite, the
system enforces a data

24
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:21.480
ceiling. Responses are capped under 40
words and choices limited

25
00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:22.840
to three options.

26
00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:26.680
For an ADHD brain, impatience with slow
response times is

27
00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:30.920
a documented neurological trait, known as
delay aversion, not merely

28
00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:35.000
a preference. Voice data streams from
Twilio, gets transcribed by

29
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.160
Deepgram, hits the cognitive loop, and
returns via 11 laps.

30
00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:43.320
Adaptive silence detection extends the
listening window during pauses.

31
00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.080
Simultaneously, natural fillers mask
processing latency.

32
00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:50.760
The entire trip is mathematically locked
at an 800 millisecond

33
00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:55.120
target. These exact parameters natively
support the processing speed of

34
00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.800
the ADHD brain rather than demanding the
caller adapt to

35
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.960
the limitations of the technology.

36
00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.200
Everyday conversational scaffolding works
for standard calls, but a separate

37
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.800
protocol is required for the exact moment
a discussion escalates

38
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.720
into a potential emergency.

39
00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:14.960
To prevent a hallucinated or misjudged
response to alarming speech,

40
00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:18.080
the large language models are completely
locked out of crisis

41
00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:23.680
management. NeuroConnect's deterministic
engine uses hard-coded regex patterns calculated

42
00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.400
to recognize ADHD distress syntax.

43
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.520
It scans transcripts and matches threat
patterns in under 10

44
00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:34.640
milliseconds. Bypassing the AI entirely, a
pre-written safety script takes

45
00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.040
over and lifeline numbers are read aloud.

46
00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.560
As a final layer of security, an automated
webhook fires

47
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.280
an alert, looping in human responders.

48
00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:48.000
Building a fail-proof crisis system for
neurodivergent individuals requires stripping

49
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.320
the AI of its autonomy the moment safety
is questioned.

50
00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:56.520
Beyond immediate crisis mitigation, the
system serves a long-term utility,

51
00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:01.480
managing the heavy administrative burdens
that often accompany neurodivergent life.

52
00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:05.720
When the caller explicitly gives their
consent, these everyday conversations

53
00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:09.880
are mined to extract functional capacity
indicators required for the

54
00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.360
National Disability Insurance Scheme.

55
00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:16.040
This diagram illustrates how the extracted
evidence is mapped to

56
00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.040
specific support domains and securely
logged into a local Postgres

57
00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:24.120
database, creating a reliable record for
future plan reviews.

58
00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.760
The privacy protocol is uncompromising.

59
00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.000
Without explicit user consent, nothing
from the interaction is ever

60
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:35.240
stored. True accessibility in the AI era
is not achieved

61
00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:36.920
by writing better prompts.

62
00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:42.200
Instead, it requires completely
redesigning the entire underlying technological stack

63
00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:46.880
to flawlessly match the exact biological
reality of the neurodivergent

64
00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:47.760
user.

